{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And they baked the dough\"</b> is that they baked it as matzot because of the commandment they were commanded: \"No se'or shall be found in your houses, for whoever eats hametzet shall be cut off.\"" "And he says <b>\"because they were driven out of Egypt\"</b>, to say that they baked it on the way because they were driven out of Egypt and could not delay to bake it in the city and to carry it baked as matzot. Therefore they carried it as dough, and their kneading bowls bound up in their garments upon their shoulders, and they hurried and baked it before it leavened, on the way or in Sukkot, when they arrived there for a brief moment, according to the words of our Sages (Mekhilta here):"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:06:50.125054127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}